 "notes": [
  "The circuit image shows 10 discrete red LEDs, so ten `led` parts are used instead of the led-bar-graph part.",
  "Each LED anode sits in the upper half of its breadboard column (columns 4, 6, 8 ... 22). Its cathode goes into the top ground rail (tn). A 220 ohm resistor bridges the centre gap in the same column. A jumper wire from the lower half of that column goes to Arduino pins 11 down to 2.",
  "Breadboard row letters follow the catalogue convention: bank 't' holds rows a-e and bank 'b' holds rows f-j, with e and f next to the centre gap. Exact holes were estimated from the image.",
  "Rail hole numbers (tn.N) are approximate. All holes on a rail are one strip, so only the distinct holes matter, not their exact numbers.",
  "The potentiometer wiper (SIG) is in the upper half at column 28. GND and VCC are in the lower half at columns 27 and 29. GND is wired to the ground rail and VCC to Arduino 5V. SIG is wired to A0.",
  "Wire colours (blue/green alternating on the LED wires) are cosmetic."
 ],
